---
/*
 * POPIA section 18 notice.
 * DRAFT: this notice MUST be reviewed by someone qualified in POPIA before launch,
 * including retention periods, cross-border transfer wording and the hosting provider's
 * logging and monitoring. Update `privacy.lastUpdated` in src/config/site.ts whenever it changes.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DataTable from '../components/DataTable.astro';
import ExternalLink from '../components/ExternalLink.astro';
import Notice from '../components/Notice.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Value from '../components/Value.astro';
import { coach } from '../config/coach';
import { registrationLine, site } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="How the Pholoso Afrika Foundation collects, uses and protects personal information under POPIA, and your rights."
>
  <PageHero
    title="Privacy notice"
    lead="We collect as little as we can, use it only for the reason you gave it, and never sell it."
  >
    <Notice variant="warning" title="Draft under review">
      <p>This notice is being reviewed and may change. Last updated: {site.privacy.lastUpdated}.</p>
    </Notice>
  </PageHero>

  <Section narrow>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Who is responsible for your information</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} ({registrationLine}) is responsible for personal information collected through
        this website.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          Address: <Value value={site.address} />
        </li>
        <li>
          Information Officer: <Value value={site.informationOfficer.name} />
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we collect, when and why</h2>
      <DataTable
        caption="Personal information we collect"
        columns={['When', 'What we collect', 'Why']}
        rows={[
          [
            'You send a message',
            'Your email address and message. Your name and the topic if you give them. Your consent, and whether you confirmed you are a child’s parent or guardian.',
            'To read and reply to your message.',
          ],
          [
            'You sign up for updates',
            'Your email address and your consent, with the date.',
            'To send the updates you asked for.',
          ],
          [
            'You request a Section 18A receipt',
            'Donor type, name, trading name, ID, passport or registration number, income tax number, address, email, phone, amount, date paid, payment reference and notes.',
            'To issue your receipt and report it to SARS, as the law requires.',
          ],
          [
            'You share a story',
            'What you choose to tell us in your message.',
            'To publish your story under a pseudonym, only with your agreement.',
          ],
          [
            'You send a child’s drawing for the Kids’ World gallery',
            'The drawing, the first name or nickname and age to show with it, your email address, and your confirmation that you are the child’s parent or guardian and agree.',
            'To show the drawing in the gallery, only with your agreement. You can ask us to remove it at any time.',
          ],
        ]}
      />
      <p>
        To limit spam, the form handler briefly keeps a scrambled one-way code made from your
        internet (IP) address, and how many messages it has sent recently. It does not keep the
        address itself.
      </p>

      <h2>You choose what to give us</h2>
      <p>
        Giving us information is voluntary. If you leave out a required answer, we cannot reply to
        your message, send you updates or issue a Section 18A receipt. Please do not include a
        child's full name or medical details. We do not need them to help you.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        You do not need to give us any information about a child to use this website. If a message
        is about a child, we ask you to confirm that you are their parent or legal guardian and that
        you agree to share the information.
      </p>
      <p>
        Kids’ World collects nothing from children. It has no forms, accounts, chat or sign-ups. The
        feelings check-in and games keep nothing, except the comfort and sound settings a child
        chooses, which stay in their own browser. Only a parent or guardian can send a child’s
        drawing for the gallery.
      </p>

      <h2>Who receives your information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>SARS</strong> receives the details on Section 18A receipts, because the law
          requires us to report them.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Microsoft 365</strong> delivers and stores the emails your form submissions
          become.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Our web host, {site.hostingProvider},</strong> runs this website. Its servers may
          be outside South Africa, and it may keep standard server logs, such as IP address, date
          and page requested, for security.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This means information you send through this website may be processed outside South Africa.
        We do not sell or rent personal information to anyone.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep Section 18A receipt records for at least five years, as tax law requires. We are
        confirming how long we keep messages and sign-ups as part of reviewing this notice. Until
        then, you can ask us at any time to delete your message or remove you from updates.
      </p>
      <p>
        Personal information sent through forms is emailed to us. It is not stored on the web
        server.
      </p>

      {
        /* Shown only when the Parent Coach is open (COACH_MODE=live). DRAFT for the POPIA
         review: processor named, cross-border transfer, children's health information (special
         personal information, processed with the parent's consent), 30-day retention. */
        coach.mode === 'live' && (
          <>
            <h2>The Parent Coach</h2>
            <p>
              The {coach.name} is a coaching conversation for parents and caregivers. When you use
              it, we keep:
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li>
                what you tell it during onboarding: your first name or nickname, your children’s
                first names or nicknames and ages, and any learning and thinking differences you
                choose (this can be health information about your child, so we ask for your
                agreement before you start);
              </li>
              <li>the conversation, your ratings and any feedback you give.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              We remove ID numbers, phone numbers and email addresses from what you type before
              anything is stored or sent. To write each reply, your messages and the details above
              are sent to <strong>Anthropic</strong>, a company in the United States that provides
              the AI. This is a transfer of personal information outside South Africa, for the sole
              purpose of writing the coach’s replies.
            </p>
            <p>
              A conversation is kept on our database for 30 days, so you can come back to it, and is
              then deleted automatically, with its feedback and rating. Anyone with the
              conversation’s web address can open it, so do not share that address.
            </p>
            <p>
              If you use voice input, your browser may send your voice to its maker to turn it into
              text. We never receive or record your voice.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>Saving your coaching is optional.</strong> If you choose to save it, we keep
              your email address so we can send you a sign-in link (there is no password), and we
              keep your saved conversations until you delete them. If you ask for a reminder, we
              email you once, a few days later; every reminder has a link to stop them. You can
              delete any saved conversation, or your whole account and everything in it, yourself on
              the My coaching page.
            </p>
          </>
        )
      }

      <h2 id="cookies">Cookies, tracking and your settings</h2>
      <p>
        This website does not use tracking cookies, advertising trackers or analytics. Comfort &
        access settings are saved only in your own browser, on your device. So is whether you have
        closed the cookie note on the home page. We never receive them.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Parent Guide works the same way. If you give it a name or your child’s interests in its
        settings, they are saved only in your browser, and you can clear them at any time. What you
        tap or type in the guide is not sent to us or to anyone else.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our current hosting service may add its own monitoring script. We have asked the host to
        confirm what it collects and to switch it off. Until that is confirmed, we cannot promise
        the live website is free of third-party monitoring.
      </p>
      <p>
        "Listen" uses the voice built into your browser or device. Some browsers send the text being
        read to their own online voice service. That text is our page content, not information about
        you.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under the Protection of Personal Information Act (POPIA), you can ask to see the information
        we hold about you, ask us to correct or delete it, and object to how we use it. You can
        withdraw your consent to updates at any time. Email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are not happy with how we handle your information, you can complain to the
        Information Regulator:{' '}
        <ExternalLink href="https://inforegulator.org.za/">inforegulator.org.za</ExternalLink>.
      </p>
      <p>Last updated: {site.privacy.lastUpdated}.</p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
